# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment template — copy to .env (NEVER commit the real .env)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PostgreSQL connection string.
#
# LOCAL DEV (embedded Postgres started via `npm run db:postgres`):
#   postgresql://hive_importer:hive_importer_dev_pw@127.0.0.1:54329/hive_importer
#
# SUPABASE (production):
#   Use the **transaction pooler** connection string (port 6543, pgbouncer) for the app
#   runtime. On serverless (Vercel) keep connection_limit small (3–5) and add
#   pool_timeout — connection_limit=1 times out under concurrent requests:
#   DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=5&pool_timeout=30"
#   ...and the **direct** connection (db.<project-ref>.supabase.co, port 5432) for migrations.
#   NOTE: the direct host is IPv6-only on the free plan — run `prisma migrate deploy`
#   from a machine/network with IPv6, or enable Supabase's IPv4 add-on.
#   DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:<password>@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres"
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://hive_importer:hive_importer_dev_pw@127.0.0.1:54329/hive_importer"

# Supabase-specific: direct (non-pooled) URL used by `prisma migrate` only.
# Not used in local dev; required on Supabase (see docs/deploy-vercel.md).
# DIRECT_URL=""
